{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# gl(3), L=2, adjoint x adjoint: the site-1 rotation on the SoV vacuum as ladder-1 Q-brackets (2026-10-10)\n\nImplements `L2-210-site1-rotation-brackets-spec.md`.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 0. Setup and regression\n\nCompanion frame, gl(3) adjoint, L=2, h=1/2, theta=(2/7,-3/5), z=(3/2,5/4,2/3). Setup cells adapted from `L2-rotation-sov.wb` cells 2-7 and 16-21 (only the dual Q's are rebuilt; the direct Q's and w-vacuum are not needed). Eigenstates at prec=60, everything downstream exact.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "Quiet[ClearAll[\"Global`*\"]];\n(* GT basis and gl(3) generators, verbatim from L2-rotation-sov.wb *)\nps[rep_] := ps[rep] = Block[{res = (Prepend[rep, #1] &) /@ Tuples[Table[Range[rep[[1, i + 1]], rep[[1, i]]], {i, 1, Length[rep[[1]]] - 1}]]}, If[Length[res[[1, 1]]] == 1, Reverse[Sort[res]], Reverse[Sort[Flatten[ps /@ res, 1]]]]];\ndim[rep_] := dim[rep] = Length[ps[{rep}]];\nJ0[k_][pat_] := J0[k][pat] = Sum[pat[[k, i]], {i, 1, k}] - Sum[pat[[k - 1, i]], {i, 1, k - 1}];\nJp[k_][pat_] := Jp[k][pat] = -Sum[(Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k + 1, j]] + j, {j, Range[k + 1]}]/Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k, j]] + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}])*v[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} -> pat[[k, i]] + 1]], {i, 1, k}];\nJm[k_][pat_] := Jm[k][pat] = Sum[(Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k - 1, j]] + j, {j, Range[k - 1]}]/Product[pat[[k, i]] - i - pat[[k, j]] + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}])*v[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} -> pat[[k, i]] - 1]], {i, 1, k}];\nJJ[k_, l_, rep_] := JJ[k, l, rep] = Which[\n  k == l, DiagonalMatrix[J0[k] /@ ps[{rep}]],\n  l == k + 1, Transpose[Table[(Coefficient[Jp[k][ps[{rep}][[i]]], v[#1]] &) /@ ps[{rep}], {i, 1, Length[ps[{rep}]]}]],\n  l == k - 1, Transpose[Table[(Coefficient[Jm[l][ps[{rep}][[i]]], v[#1]] &) /@ ps[{rep}], {i, 1, Length[ps[{rep}]]}]],\n  l > k + 1, JJ[k, k + 1, rep] . JJ[k + 1, l, rep] - JJ[k + 1, l, rep] . JJ[k, k + 1, rep],\n  l < k - 1, JJ[k, k - 1, rep] . JJ[k - 1, l, rep] - JJ[k - 1, l, rep] . JJ[k, k - 1, rep]];\nchecks = <||>;\nΛ = {2, 1, 0}; nL = 2; d1 = dim[Λ]; d2 = d1^nL; id2 = IdentityMatrix[d2];\nhN = 1/2; thN = {2/7, -3/5}; zN = {3/2, 5/4, 2/3}; prec = 60;\nEe[i_, j_] := Ee[i, j] = JJ[i, j, Λ];\nE1[i_, j_] := E1[i, j] = KroneckerProduct[Ee[i, j], IdentityMatrix[d1]];\nE2[i_, j_] := E2[i, j] = KroneckerProduct[IdentityMatrix[d1], Ee[i, j]];\nwtBasis = Flatten[Table[Table[J0[k][p1] + J0[k][p2], {k, 3}], {p1, ps[{Λ}]}, {p2, ps[{Λ}]}], 1];\nnuP[n_][x_] := Product[x - thN[[s]] + hN Λ[[n]], {s, nL}];\n(* monodromy at a numeric argument v, twist on the right, quantum minors *)\nTm[v_] := Tm[v] = Table[Sum[(KroneckerDelta[i, k] (v - thN[[1]]) id2 + hN E1[i, k]) . (KroneckerDelta[k, j] (v - thN[[2]]) id2 + hN E2[k, j]), {k, 3}], {i, 3}, {j, 3}];\nTMf[M_][i_, j_][v_] := Sum[Tm[v][[i, l]] M[[l, j]], {l, 3}];\nqminor[M_][I_, J_][v_] := Sum[Signature[σ] Dot @@ Table[TMf[M][σ[[k]], J[[k]]][v - (k - 1) hN], {k, Length[J]}], {σ, Permutations[I]}];\ntAt[M_, a_, v_] := Sum[qminor[M][I, I][v], {I, Subsets[Range[3], {a}]}];\nuS = 1/7 + Range[0, 6]/3;\ntPoly[M_, a_] := Expand[Sum[tAt[M, a, uS[[k]]] Product[(u - uS[[l]])/(uS[[k]] - uS[[l]]), {l, DeleteCases[Range[7], k]}], {k, 7}]];\nZd = DiagonalMatrix[zN]; χ3z = Times @@ zN;\n{tTime, tZ} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[tPoly[Zd, a], {a, 3}]];\nchecks[\"qdet: t3 = chi3 nu1(u) nu2(u-h) nu3(u-2h)\"] = Union[Flatten[Expand[tZ[[3]] - χ3z nuP[1][u] nuP[2][u - hN] nuP[3][u - 2 hN] id2]]] === {0};\n{tTime, checks}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "maxc[e_, var_] := Max[Abs[Flatten[CoefficientList[Chop[Expand[e], 10^-40], var]]], 0];\nsectors = GatherBy[Range[d2], wtBasis[[#]] &];\nmixN = N[(tZ[[1]] + Pi tZ[[2]]) /. u -> 3/7, prec];\nstates = Flatten[Table[With[{es = Eigensystem[mixN[[sec, sec]]]}, Table[<|\"mu\" -> wtBasis[[sec[[1]]]], \"ev\" -> es[[1, r]], \"vec\" -> Normal[SparseArray[Thread[sec -> es[[2, r]]], {d2}]]|>, {r, Length[sec]}]], {sec, sectors}], 1];\nnS = Length[states]; muS = states[[All, \"mu\"]]; vecS = states[[All, \"vec\"]];\ntZn = N[tZ, prec];\nvals = Table[With[{k = Ordering[Abs[ψ], -1][[1]]}, Table[Chop[Expand[(tZn[[a]] . ψ)[[k]]/ψ[[k]]], 10^-40], {a, 3}]], {ψ, vecS}];\nchecks[\"64 eigenvectors of t1,t2,t3 (max residual)\"] = Max[Table[maxc[tZn[[a]] . vecS[[A]] - vals[[A, a]] vecS[[A]], u], {A, nS}, {a, 3}]];\n{nS, N[checks[\"64 eigenvectors of t1,t2,t3 (max residual)\"], 3]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* dual Q-operator (Baxter) equation; only the dual Q's are used below *)\nopDual[tt_, Q_, x_] := nuP[3][x] nuP[3][x - hN] nuP[3][x - 2 hN] Q[x + hN] - (tt[[1]] /. u -> x) nuP[3][x - hN] nuP[3][x - 2 hN] Q[x] + (tt[[2]] /. u -> x) nuP[3][x - 2 hN] Q[x - hN] - (tt[[3]] /. u -> x) Q[x - 2 hN];\n(* minimal-degree monic q with Q = zz^(s x/h) q solving op; empty list if none up to degree 6 *)\nsolveQ[op_, tt_, zz_, s_] := Module[{c, eqs, ns, res = {}},\n  Do[If[res === {},\n    eqs = CoefficientList[Chop[Expand[op[tt, Function[yy, zz^(s (yy - X)/hN) Sum[c[j] yy^j, {j, 0, d}]], X]], 10^-40], X];\n    ns = If[eqs === {}, {UnitVector[d + 1, d + 1]}, NullSpace[N[Table[Coefficient[e, c[j]], {e, eqs}, {j, 0, d}], prec], Tolerance -> 10^-30]];\n    If[Length[ns] > 0, res = Expand[#/Coefficient[#, X, d]] &[Sum[ns[[1, j + 1]] X^j, {j, 0, d}]]]], {d, 0, 6}]; res];\n{qTime, qu} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[solveQ[opDual, vals[[A]], zN[[j]], 1], {A, nS}, {j, 3}]];\nchecks[\"all dual Q's found\"] = FreeQ[qu, {}];\nchecks[\"deg q^j = mu_j - L lambda3\"] = And @@ Flatten[Table[Exponent[qu[[A, j]], X] == muS[[A, j]] - nL Λ[[3]], {A, nS}, {j, 3}]];\n{qTime, checks[\"all dual Q's found\"], checks[\"deg q^j = mu_j - L lambda3\"]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* poles, physical-space Gauss factors, SoV vacuum x0 = (e1^T Pphys^-1)^{tensor 2}; symbols z[i], r[i], s[i] as in the reference *)\nQU[A_, j_, x_] := QU[A, j, x] = N[zN[[j]]^(x/hN), prec] (qu[[A, j]] /. X -> x);\nrsSol = {s[1] -> z[1]^2/((z[1] - z[2]) (z[1] - z[3])), s[2] -> -(z[2]/(z[1] (z[2] - z[3]))), s[3] -> 1/(z[1] z[2]), r[1] -> -(z[3]/z[2]), r[2] -> -(z[3]/z[1]), r[3] -> (z[2]^2 (-z[1] + z[3]))/(z[1]^2 (z[2] - z[3]))};\nnumZ = Thread[{z[1], z[2], z[3]} -> zN];\nrsN = rsSol /. numZ;\nPpp = MatrixExp[(1/zN[[1]]) Ee[1, 2]] . MatrixExp[-(1/(zN[[1]] zN[[2]])) Ee[1, 3]] . MatrixExp[((zN[[1]] + zN[[2]])/(zN[[1]] zN[[2]])) Ee[2, 3]];\nPmp = MatrixExp[(r[1] /. rsN) Ee[3, 2]] . MatrixExp[(r[2] /. rsN) Ee[3, 1]] . MatrixExp[(r[3] /. rsN) Ee[2, 1]];\nPdp = DiagonalMatrix[Table[Product[(s[k] /. rsN)^J0[k][p], {k, 3}], {p, ps[{Λ}]}]];\nPph1 = Pmp . Pdp . Ppp; PphInv1 = Inverse[Pph1];\nx01 = First[{UnitVector[d1, 1]} . PphInv1]; x02 = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[x01, x01]];\nx0ovl = Table[x02 . vecS[[B]], {B, nS}];\nchecks[\"<x0|Psi_B> nonzero (min, not a zero test)\"] = Min[Abs[x0ovl]];\nN[checks[\"<x0|Psi_B> nonzero (min, not a zero test)\"], 4]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* untwisted L=2 B(u) in the GT product basis (= companion frame) and the L=1 SoV covectors (constants, from Rotation-e8-SoV Section 1) *)\nId3 = IdentityMatrix[3];\nBop2[v_] := TMf[Id3][1, 1][v] . qminor[Id3][{1, 2}, {1, 2}][v + hN] + TMf[Id3][2, 1][v] . qminor[Id3][{1, 2}, {1, 3}][v + hN];\ngtpats = {{{2}, {2, 1}}, {{2}, {1, 1}}, {{1}, {1, 1}}, {{2}, {2, 0}}, {{2}, {1, 0}}, {{2}, {0, 0}}, {{1}, {1, 0}}, {{1}, {0, 0}}};\nuv = UnitVector[d1, #] &;\nxL1 = {uv[1], hN (uv[2] + uv[3]), 6 hN^2 uv[5], hN uv[2], 2 hN^2 uv[4], hN^3 (-3 uv[6] + 4 uv[7]), 9 hN^3 uv[6], 9 hN^4 uv[8]};\n(* full L=2 SoV basis: left eigenvectors of the untwisted B, labelled by their 6 roots in units of h relative to theta_s *)\nBpoly = Expand[Sum[Bop2[uS[[k]]] Product[(u - uS[[l]])/(uS[[k]] - uS[[l]]), {l, DeleteCases[Range[7], k]}], {k, 7}]];\nchecks[\"B(u) degree 6 and interpolation exact\"] = (Max[Exponent[Bpoly, u]] == 6) && (Union[Flatten[Expand[(Bpoly /. u -> 19/23) - Bop2[19/23]]]] === {0});\n{evB, vecB} = Eigensystem[Transpose[N[Bpoly /. u -> 3/11, prec]]];\nchecks[\"B simple spectrum (min gap)\"] = Min[Abs[Subtract @@@ Subsets[evB, {2}]]];\nrootsOf[c_] := Module[{k = First[Ordering[Abs[c], -1]], ev}, ev = Chop[Expand[(c . N[Bpoly, prec])[[k]]/c[[k]]], 10^-30];\n   Sort[Chop[u /. NSolve[ev == 0, u, WorkingPrecision -> 40], 10^-20]]];\nsovRoots = Table[rootsOf[c], {c, vecB}];\nladderOf[r_] := Module[{t1 = (r - thN[[1]])/hN, t2 = (r - thN[[2]])/hN}, Which[Abs[t1 - Round[t1]] < 10^-15, {1, Round[t1]}, Abs[t2 - Round[t2]] < 10^-15, {2, Round[t2]}, True, {0, r}]];\nlab[m_] := {Sort[Map[Last, Select[ladderOf /@ sovRoots[[m]], First[#] == 1 &]]], Sort[Map[Last, Select[ladderOf /@ sovRoots[[m]], First[#] == 2 &]]]};\n{checks[\"B(u) degree 6 and interpolation exact\"], N[checks[\"B simple spectrum (min gap)\"], 3], Tally[lab /@ Range[64]] // Length}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* site-1 rotation in the companion frame: (e1^T rho(g)) tensor e1^T, generic g, expanded in the L=2 SoV basis *)\nωg = {{-1/5, 2/7, -1/3}, {3/4, 1/6, -2/9}, {1/8, -3/5, 2/11}};\nρg = MatrixExp[N[Sum[ωg[[i, j]] Ee[i, j], {i, 3}, {j, 3}], prec]];\nΦsite1 = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[uv[1] . ρg, uv[1]]];\ncSoV = LinearSolve[Transpose[vecB], Φsite1];\ncheckExp = Norm[cSoV . vecB - Φsite1]/Norm[Φsite1];\nsupp = Select[Range[64], Abs[cSoV[[#]]]/Max[Abs[cSoV]] > 10^-30 &];\nchecks[\"site-1 rotation: # SoV states in support\"] = Length[supp];\n(* companion-frame kets and the L=2 SoV wavefunction in terms of the dual Q values *)\nPinv2 = KroneckerProduct[PphInv1, PphInv1];\nketC = Table[N[Pinv2 . vecS[[B]], prec], {B, nS}];\nx0C = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[uv[1], uv[1]]];\nchecks[\"companion kets: <x0|Psi> = diag-frame <x0|Psi>\"] = Max[Abs[Table[x0C . ketC[[B]] - x0ovl[[B]], {B, nS}]]]/Min[Abs[x0ovl]];\ncolV2[B_, s_, m_] := Table[QU[B, j, thN[[s]] + m hN], {j, 3}];\npsiSite[B_, s_, {m1_, m21_, m22_}, {a_, b_}, k_] := (colV2[B, s, m21][[a]] colV2[B, s, m1][[b]] - colV2[B, s, m21][[b]] colV2[B, s, m1][[a]]) colV2[B, s, m22][[k]];\npsiPred[B_, m_, rows_, k_] := Product[psiSite[B, s, lab[m][[s]], rows, k], {s, nL}];\npsiAt0[B_, rows_, k_] := Product[psiSite[B, s, {-3, -2, -1}, rows, k], {s, nL}];\nwfRatio[rows_, k_] := Table[Module[{r = Table[((vecB[[m]] . ketC[[B]])/(x0C . ketC[[B]]))/(psiPred[B, m, rows, k]/psiAt0[B, rows, k]), {B, nS}]}, Max[Abs[r/r[[1]] - 1]]], {m, 64}];\nwf12 = wfRatio[{1, 2}, 1];\nchecks[\"L=2 SoV wavefunction = prod_s det2[v(x21),v(x1)] v_k(x22), max over 64 SoV states\"] = Max[wf12];\n{N[checkExp, 3], Length[supp], N[checks[\"companion kets: <x0|Psi> = diag-frame <x0|Psi>\"], 3], N[Max[wf12], 3]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* state-independent SoV normalisations N_m; lambda_2; site-1 wavefunction; the 12-state sum *)\nNm = Table[((vecB[[m]] . ketC[[1]])/(x0C . ketC[[1]]))/(psiPred[1, m, {1, 2}, 1]/psiAt0[1, {1, 2}, 1]), {m, 64}];\nchecks[\"v(theta_s) parallel v(theta_s - h) at L=2\"] = Max[Table[Norm[Flatten[Minors[Transpose[{colV2[B, s, 0], colV2[B, s, -1]}], 2]]]/(Norm[colV2[B, s, 0]] Norm[colV2[B, s, -1]]), {B, nS}, {s, nL}]];\nλ2[B_] := colV2[B, 2, 0][[1]]/colV2[B, 2, -1][[1]];\npsi1[B_, t_] := psiSite[B, 1, t, {1, 2}, 1]/psiSite[B, 1, {-3, -2, -1}, {1, 2}, 1];\nqRep[B_] := Sum[cSoV[[m]] Nm[[m]] psi1[B, lab[m][[1]]] If[lab[m][[2]] == {-3, -2, -1}, 1, λ2[B]], {m, supp}];\nchecks[\"site-1 rotation: <Phi|Psi>/<x0|Psi> = sum over the 12 SoV states of Q-dets (max rel dev, 64 states)\"] = Max[Table[Abs[(Φsite1 . ketC[[B]])/(x0C . ketC[[B]])/qRep[B] - 1], {B, nS}]];\ncL1 = (uv[1] . ρg) . Inverse[N[xL1, prec]];\ntrip = {{-3, -2, -1}, {-3, -1, -1}, {-2, -1, -1}, {-3, -2, 0}, {-3, -1, 0}, {-3, 0, 0}, {-2, -1, 0}, {-2, 0, 0}};\n{Length[supp], Union[lab[#][[2]] & /@ supp], N[checks[\"v(theta_s) parallel v(theta_s - h) at L=2\"], 3], N[checks[\"site-1 rotation: <Phi|Psi>/<x0|Psi> = sum over the 12 SoV states of Q-dets (max rel dev, 64 states)\"], 3]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* the linear map K: L=1 SoV covector x_nu tensor e1 -> L=2 SoV states, in normalised-wavefunction units *)\nKrow[ν_] := Module[{c = LinearSolve[Transpose[vecB], N[Flatten[KroneckerProduct[xL1[[ν]], uv[1]]], prec]] Nm}, Select[Table[{lab[m], c[[m]]}, {m, 64}], Abs[#[[2]]] > 10^-30 &]];\n(* 2-plane data per state: v(theta1-h) = alpha v(theta1-3h) + beta v(theta1-2h); lambda_s = v_k(theta_s)/v_k(theta_s-h) *)\nvv[B_, s_, m_] := colV2[B, s, m];\nabSolve[B_] := Module[{M = Transpose[{vv[B, 1, -3], vv[B, 1, -2]}], sol}, sol = LeastSquares[M, vv[B, 1, -1]]; {sol, Norm[M . sol - vv[B, 1, -1]]/Norm[vv[B, 1, -1]]}];\nabData = Table[abSolve[B], {B, nS}];\nchecks[\"v(theta1-h) in span{v(theta1-3h), v(theta1-2h)} (max residual)\"] = Max[abData[[All, 2]]];\nαB = abData[[All, 1, 1]]; βB = abData[[All, 1, 2]];\nλ1B = Table[vv[B, 1, 0][[1]]/vv[B, 1, -1][[1]], {B, nS}]; λ2B = Table[λ2[B], {B, nS}];\npsiAB[B_] := With[{a = αB[[B]], b = βB[[B]], l = λ1B[[B]]}, {1, b, -a, l, l b, l^2 b, -l a, -l^2 a}];\nchecks[\"8 site-1 wavefunctions = {1,beta,-alpha} x {1,lambda1,lambda1^2} (max rel dev)\"] = Max[Table[Abs[psi1[B, trip[[i]]]/psiAB[B][[i]] - 1], {B, nS}, {i, 8}]];\ntripIdx[t_] := First[FirstPosition[trip, t]];\npsiSym = {1, β, -α, λ1, λ1 β, λ1^2 β, -λ1 α, -λ1^2 α};\nKrat[ν_] := {#[[1]], Rationalize[Chop[#[[2]], 10^-40], 10^-30]} & /@ Krow[ν];\nchecks[\"K rationalization error\"] = Max[Table[Abs[Krat[ν][[i, 2]] - Krow[ν][[i, 2]]], {ν, 8}, {i, Length[Krow[ν]]}]];\nKmat[s2_] := Table[With[{sel = Select[Krat[ν], #[[1]] == {trip[[x]], s2} &]}, If[sel === {}, 0, sel[[1, 2]]]], {ν, 8}, {x, 8}];\nKvac = Kmat[{-3, -2, -1}]; K20 = Kmat[{-3, -2, 0}];\nchecks[\"Kvac rank\"] = MatrixRank[Kvac]; checks[\"K20 rank\"] = MatrixRank[K20];\n(* every Krat entry lands in Kvac or K20 (12-state support) *)\nchecks[\"all K support in the two site-2 columns\"] = (Total[Length[Krat[#]] & /@ Range[8]] == Count[Flatten[Kvac], Except[0]] + Count[Flatten[K20], Except[0]]);\n{N[checks[\"v(theta1-h) in span{v(theta1-3h), v(theta1-2h)} (max residual)\"], 3], N[checks[\"8 site-1 wavefunctions = {1,beta,-alpha} x {1,lambda1,lambda1^2} (max rel dev)\"], 3], N[checks[\"K rationalization error\"], 3], MatrixRank[Kvac], MatrixRank[K20], checks[\"all K support in the two site-2 columns\"]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* equivariant linear map X: GT-basis covectors -> 3x3 matrices, rebuilt by solving the equivariance condition linearly (the variant with 1-dim null space is the right one) *)\nee[i_, j_] := Table[KroneckerDelta[i, ii] KroneckerDelta[j, jj], {ii, 3}, {jj, 3}];\nxvars = Flatten[Table[xx[ν, p, q], {ν, 8}, {p, 3}, {q, 3}]];\nXof[φ_] := Sum[φ[[ν]] Table[xx[ν, p, q], {p, 3}, {q, 3}], {ν, 8}];\nEtr[a_, b_] := Ee[a, b] - KroneckerDelta[a, b] IdentityMatrix[d1];\nequivEqs[ε_, tr_] := Flatten[Table[Xof[UnitVector[8, k] . Etr[a, b]] - ε (Xof[UnitVector[8, k]] . tr[ee[a, b]] - tr[ee[a, b]] . Xof[UnitVector[8, k]]), {k, 8}, {a, 3}, {b, 3}]];\nnullDims = Flatten[Table[{ε, tr, Length[NullSpace[Table[Coefficient[e, v], {e, equivEqs[ε, tr]}, {v, xvars}]]]}, {ε, {1, -1}}, {tr, {Identity, Transpose}}], 1];\ngood = First[Select[nullDims, Last[#] == 1 &]];\nXsol = First[NullSpace[Table[Coefficient[e, v], {e, equivEqs[good[[1]], good[[2]]]}, {v, xvars}]]];\nXmat[φ_] := Xof[φ] /. Thread[xvars -> Xsol];\nXc[cvec_] := Xmat[cvec . xL1];\nrank1dev[M_] := With[{s = SingularValueList[N[M, 30]]}, If[Length[s] < 2, 0, s[[2]]/s[[1]]]];\nSeedRandom[7]; cRnd = RandomInteger[{-9, 9}, 8];\nexactOvl[cvec_, B_] := (Flatten[KroneckerProduct[cvec . xL1, uv[1]]] . ketC[[B]])/(x0C . ketC[[B]]);\nsubsB[B_] := {α -> αB[[B]], β -> βB[[B]], λ1 -> λ1B[[B]], λ2 -> λ2B[[B]]};\nWsym[ν_] := Sum[kx[[2]] psiSym[[tripIdx[kx[[1, 1]]]]] If[kx[[1, 2]] == {-3, -2, -1}, 1, λ2], {kx, Krat[ν]}];\nRsym = Sum[c[ν] Wsym[ν], {ν, 8}];\nchecks[\"Rsym = exact overlap, rotation c=cL1 (max rel dev)\"] = Max[Table[Abs[(Rsym /. Thread[Array[c, 8] -> cL1] /. subsB[B])/exactOvl[cL1, B] - 1], {B, nS}]];\nchecks[\"Rsym = exact overlap, random c (max rel dev)\"] = Max[Table[Abs[(Rsym /. Thread[Array[c, 8] -> cRnd] /. subsB[B])/exactOvl[cRnd, B] - 1], {B, nS}]];\nchecks[\"X(e1) rank 1, traceless\"] = {rank1dev[Xmat[UnitVector[8, 1]]], Tr[Xmat[UnitVector[8, 1]]]};\nchecks[\"X(cL1) rank 1 (rotation, 2nd/1st singular value)\"] = rank1dev[Xc[cL1]];\nchecks[\"X(random c) 2nd/1st singular value (should be O(1))\"] = rank1dev[Xc[cRnd]];\n{nullDims, N[{checks[\"Rsym = exact overlap, rotation c=cL1 (max rel dev)\"], checks[\"Rsym = exact overlap, random c (max rel dev)\"], checks[\"X(cL1) rank 1 (rotation, 2nd/1st singular value)\"], checks[\"X(random c) 2nd/1st singular value (should be O(1))\"]}, 3], Xmat[UnitVector[8, 1]]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* rotation covectors parametrised by X = a b^T (b.a = 0): the c-vector is the unique linear-in-(a b^T) covector with X(c) = traceless part of a b^T, which equals a b^T on b.a = 0; the traceless projection makes the symbolic map polynomial and bilinear *)\nXlin = Table[Flatten[Xmat[UnitVector[8, k]]], {k, 8}];\nrotFromAB[a_, b_] := Module[{Xt = Flatten[Outer[Times, a, b] - (a . b)/3 IdentityMatrix[3]], φ}, φ = LinearSolve[Transpose[Xlin], Xt]; φ . Inverse[xL1]];\nSeedRandom[23]; abList = Table[With[{a = RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, 3], b0 = RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, 3]}, {a, b0 - (b0 . a) a/(a . a)}], {3}];\nchecks[\"rotFromAB gives rotations (2nd/1st sv)\"] = Max[rank1dev[Xc[rotFromAB @@ ab]] & /@ abList];\naS = {a1, a2, a3}; bS = {b1, b2, b3};\ncAB = rotFromAB[aS, bS];\nb3sub = b3 -> -(a1 b1 + a2 b2)/a3;\nchecks[\"X(c(a,b)) = a b^T - (a.b/3) 1, identically in (a,b)\"] = Expand[Xc[cAB] - (Outer[Times, aS, bS] - (aS . bS)/3 IdentityMatrix[3])] === ConstantArray[0, {3, 3}];\nΦvac = Together /@ (cAB . Kvac); Φ20 = Together /@ (cAB . K20);\n(* bilinearity: homogeneous of degree 1 in a and degree 1 in b separately, as polynomials *)\ntt0 = Expand[Φvac]; tt1 = Expand[Φ20];\nchecks[\"Phi_vac, Phi_20 bilinear in (a,b)\"] = And @@ (Expand[(# /. {a1 -> t a1, a2 -> t a2, a3 -> t a3}) - t #] === 0 && Expand[(# /. {b1 -> t b1, b2 -> t b2, b3 -> t b3}) - t #] === 0 & /@ Join[tt0, tt1]);\nbraTab = Join[Table[{\"site 1 \" <> ToString[trip[[x]]] <> \", site 2 vac\", Factor[Φvac[[x]]]}, {x, 8}], Table[{\"site 1 \" <> ToString[trip[[x]]] <> \", site 2 {2|20}\", Factor[Φ20[[x]]]}, {x, 8}]];\nbraTab = Select[braTab, #[[2]] =!= 0 &];\n{N[checks[\"rotFromAB gives rotations (2nd/1st sv)\"], 3], checks[\"X(c(a,b)) = a b^T - (a.b/3) 1, identically in (a,b)\"], checks[\"Phi_vac, Phi_20 bilinear in (a,b)\"], Length[braTab]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 0 results (2026-10-10, kernel evaluated via `Hlp`rc` reading this file; VS Code would not execute cells of the new notebook, so results are stored in markdown cells)\n\n| check | value |\n|---|---|\n| 64 eigenvectors of t1,t2,t3 (max residual, prec 60) | 0 (below 10^-40 chop) |\n| all 192 dual Q's found, degrees mu_j - L lambda3 | True, True (0.47 s) |\n| B(u) degree 6, interpolation exact; simple spectrum | True, min gap 1.6e-5 |\n| site-1 rotation (cell 8, generic omega): expansion in SoV basis (rel norm) | 1e-59; support = 12 SoV states, site-2 triples {-3,-2,-1}, {-3,-2,0} |\n| L=2 SoV wavefunction = prod_s det2 v_k, max over 64 SoV states | 1e-47 |\n| companion kets: <x0 vs Psi> equals diag-frame | 1e-55 |\n| 12-state sum = exact overlap, 64 states | below 1e-47 (printed 0 at prec 47) |\n| Rsym (polynomial in alpha, beta, lambda1, lambda2) = exact overlap, rotation c=cL1 and random c | below 1e-47 both |\n| v(theta1-h) in span(v(theta1-3h), v(theta1-2h)); 8 psi = {1,beta,-alpha} x {1,lambda1,lambda1^2} | 1e-51 / 1e-47 |\n| K rationalisation error | 1e-52 |\n| rank Kvac, rank K20 | 8, 4 |\n| X(cL1) rank-1 dev; X(random c) | 0 (rotation); 0.093 (random is not a rotation) |\n| rotFromAB: X(c(a,b)) = traceless part of a b^T identically; Phi_vac, Phi_20 bilinear (a,b) | True, True |\n\n**Convention fixed here (differs from the reference).** The c-vector of a rotation is built with the traceless projection X(c) = a b^T - (a.b/3) 1, which equals a b^T on b.a = 0 and makes c(a,b) a polynomial bilinear in (a,b); impose b3 = -(a1 b1 + a2 b2)/a3 only when solving loci. (The reference's un-projected symbolic solve is inconsistent when b.a is not set to zero first.)\n\nTimings: setup cells 2.5 + 0.5 + 0.5 + 1.8 + (cells 8-11: about 4 s) s; cell 12 (symbolic c(a,b), Factor) 73 s.\n\nBilinear slots (b3 free), Phi_vac = cAB.Kvac in trip order (-3,-2,-1), (-3,-1,-1), (-2,-1,-1), (-3,-2,0), (-3,-1,0), (-3,0,0), (-2,-1,0), (-2,0,0):\n\nPhi_vac = { a3 b1/3, 16 a3 b2/81, 8 (a1 b1 + a2 b2 - 2 a3 b3)/81, (62 a2 b1 + 27 a3 b2)/186, -8 (a1 b1 - a2 b2)/81, 4 a1 b2/93, (43 a1 b2 - 16 a2 b3)/81, -8 a1 b3/93 }\n\nPhi_20 = { -3395 a3 b2/5022, 0, 0, 35 (a1 b1 - a2 b2)/81, -35 a1 b2/93, 0, -280 a1 b3/2511, 0 }",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 1. The monomial table and the tensors CC0, CC1\n\nUsing `psiSite` (rows {1,2}, k=1) the ladder-1 wavefunction of a triple (m1, m21, m22) is det2[v(m21), v(m1)]_{rows} v_k(m22) with det2[p,q] = p_a q_b - p_b q_a. So with the minor (n,n') := det2[v(n'), v(n)] (n < n') and Psi1 := minor(-3,-2) v_k(-1), psi_x Psi1 = minor(n,n') v_k(r) for x = (n,n',r) = trip (the triple read as (n, n'; r)): this is exact for any row pair and any component k because v(0) is parallel to v(-1) (lambda1 independent of k).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* monomial table: psi_x Psi1 = M_x for the 8 triples, for three (rows, k) choices, all 64 states *)\ndet2[p_, q_, {a_, b_}] := p[[a]] q[[b]] - p[[b]] q[[a]];\nvm[B_, m_] := colV2[B, 1, m];\nminorQ[B_, {n_, np_}, rows_] := det2[vm[B, np], vm[B, n], rows];\nMx[B_, t_, rows_, k_] := minorQ[B, {t[[1]], t[[2]]}, rows] vm[B, t[[3]]][[k]];\nPsi1[B_, rows_, k_] := Mx[B, trip[[1]], rows, k];\ntableDev = Table[With[{rows = rk[[1]], k = rk[[2]]}, Max[Table[Abs[psiAB[B][[x]] Psi1[B, rows, k]/Mx[B, trip[[x]], rows, k] - 1], {B, nS}, {x, 8}]]], {rk, {{{1, 2}, 1}, {{2, 3}, 3}, {{1, 3}, 2}}}];\n(* and with psi1, the SoV wavefunction function of the reference, directly for rows {1,2}, k=1 *)\ntableDevPsi1 = Max[Table[Abs[psi1[B, trip[[x]]] Psi1[B, {1, 2}, 1]/Mx[B, trip[[x]], {1, 2}, 1] - 1], {B, nS}, {x, 8}]];\nchecks[\"monomial table psi_x Psi1 = M_x (max rel dev: rows12 k1, rows23 k3, rows13 k2; psi1 direct)\"] = Append[tableDev, tableDevPsi1];\n(* the tensors: minor order and columns *)\nmnL = {{-3, -2}, {-3, -1}, {-2, -1}, {-3, 0}, {-2, 0}, {-1, 0}}; rrL = {-3, -2, -1, 0};\ntensorOf[φ_] := Module[{CC = ConstantArray[0, {6, 4}]}, Do[CC[[First[First[Position[mnL, {trip[[x, 1]], trip[[x, 2]]}]]], First[First[Position[rrL, trip[[x, 3]]]]]]] = φ[[x]], {x, 8}]; CC];\nCC0 = tensorOf[Φvac]; CC1 = tensorOf[Φ20];\n(* overlap identity: <Phi|Psi>/<x0|Psi> Psi1 = sum_{nn',r} (CC0 + lambda2 CC1)_{nn',r} minor(n,n') v_k(r) *)\nbrk[B_, cc_, rows_, k_] := Sum[cc[[i, j]] minorQ[B, mnL[[i]], rows] vm[B, rrL[[j]]][[k]], {i, 6}, {j, 4}];\nabSub[ab_] := Thread[{a1, a2, a3, b1, b2, b3} -> Join[ab[[1]], ab[[2]]]];\nidDev[cvec_, ccRule_, rows_, k_] := Max[Table[With[{cc0 = CC0 /. ccRule, cc1 = CC1 /. ccRule}, Abs[exactOvl[cvec, B] Psi1[B, rows, k]/(brk[B, cc0 + λ2B[[B]] cc1, rows, k]) - 1]], {B, nS}]];\nidTab = Join[Table[idDev[rotFromAB @@ ab, abSub[ab], {1, 2}, 1], {ab, abList[[1 ;; 2]]}], {idDev[rotFromAB @@ abList[[1]], abSub[abList[[1]]], {2, 3}, 3]}];\n(* random c (a covector that is not a rotation) through the c-linear tensors *)\ncRndDev = Max[Table[Abs[exactOvl[cRnd, B] Psi1[B, {1, 2}, 1]/(brk[B, tensorOf[cRnd . Kvac] + λ2B[[B]] tensorOf[cRnd . K20], {1, 2}, 1]) - 1], {B, nS}]];\nchecks[\"overlap identity with CC0 + lambda2 CC1 (2 rotations rows12 k1; rotation rows23 k3; random c)\"] = Append[idTab, cRndDev];\ngenPt = Thread[{a1, a2, a3, b1, b2, b3} -> {3, 5, 7, 11, 13, 17}];\n(* Position at level 2 with Heads -> False: the populated (minor, r) slots *)\npopSlots[cc_] := Map[{mnL[[#[[1]]]], rrL[[#[[2]]]]} &, Position[cc /. genPt, x_ /; x =!= 0, {2}, Heads -> False]];\nStringReplace[ToString[{N[tableDev, 3], N[tableDevPsi1, 3], N[idTab, 3], N[cRndDev, 3], Length[popSlots[CC0]], Length[popSlots[CC1]], popSlots[CC0], popSlots[CC1]}, InputForm], \"\\n\" -> \" \"]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 1 results\n\n**Table (exact, all 64 states, deviation below 1e-47):** psi_x Psi1 = M_x with M_x = minor(n,n') v_k(r), minor(n,n') := det2[v(n'), v(n)] = v_a(n') v_b(n) - v_b(n') v_a(n) for n<n', Psi1 = M_(-3,-2;-1). It holds for (rows,k) = ({1,2},1), ({2,3},3), ({1,3},2) alike, and against the reference `psi1` directly (max dev about 1e-47). The triple x=(t1,t2,t3) reads as (n,n';r) = (t1,t2;t3). In the spec's det2[v(n),v(n')] with n<n' every M_x carries an overall sign -1 relative to mine (my convention is the one in which psi_x, including its sign, is the coefficient, so N0 = sum phi_x M_x with no extra signs).\n\n**Tensors** (rows = minors in order (-3,-2),(-3,-1),(-2,-1),(-3,0),(-2,0),(-1,0); columns r = -3,-2,-1,0; entries bilinear in (a,b), b3 free):\n- CC0 populated: (-3,-2;-1)=phi1, (-3,-1;-1)=phi2, (-2,-1;-1)=phi3, (-3,-2;0)=phi4, (-3,-1;0)=phi5, (-3,0;0)=phi6, (-2,-1;0)=phi7, (-2,0;0)=phi8 (8 slots; (-1,0;.) empty; columns r=-3,-2 empty).\n- CC1 populated: (-3,-2;-1), (-3,-2;0), (-3,-1;0), (-2,-1;0) (4 slots).\n- phi^0 = Phi_vac, phi^1 = Phi_20 of Task 0.\n\n**Overlap identity** <Phi|Psi>/<x0|Psi> Psi1 = sum (CC0 + lambda2 CC1)_{nn',r} minor(n,n') v_k(r): deviation 1e-48, 1e-48 (two rotations, rows12 k1), 1e-51 (rotation, rows23 k3), 1e-48 (random non-rotation c). Table time 0.46 s.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 2. Bracket dictionary and the forms (symbolic)\n\nPoints m = -3,-2,-1,0 (theta1 + m h) are indexed 1..4. Use rows (2,3) and k = 3 (the spec's ladder-1 Q^2, Q^3). Bracket <Q^j F> = sum_m F_m q[j,m]. With the orientation Bk2[F,G] := <Q^3F><Q^2G> - <Q^2F><Q^3G> one gets exactly sum_{n<n'} (F^G)_{nn'} minor_23(n,n'), (F^G)_{nn'} = F_n G_n' - F_n' G_n, so no sign appears between (F^G) and my minor convention. The 3x3 is built with columns (<Q^3F_i>, <Q^2F_i>, <Q^3H_i>).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* symbolic Q values on the four points: q[j,m], j = 1,2,3; bras Fv[i][m] free on the four points *)\nptsM = {-3, -2, -1, 0};\nqq[j_, m_] := q[j, m];\nbrQ[j_, F_] := Sum[F[[i]] qq[j, ptsM[[i]]], {i, 4}];\nBk2[F_, G_] := brQ[3, F] brQ[2, G] - brQ[2, F] brQ[3, G];\nwedge2[F_, G_] := Table[F[[mnL[[l, 1]] + 4]] G[[mnL[[l, 2]] + 4]] - F[[mnL[[l, 2]] + 4]] G[[mnL[[l, 1]] + 4]], {l, 6}];\n(* minor_23(n,n') = det2[v(n'), v(n)] on rows (2,3) = q2(n') q3(n) - q3(n') q2(n) *)\nminSym[{n_, np_}] := qq[2, np] qq[3, n] - qq[3, np] qq[2, n];\nFs = Table[Subscript[f, i, m], {i, 3}, {m, 4}]; Hs = Table[Subscript[hh, i, m], {i, 3}, {m, 4}];\nF1 = Fs[[1]]; G1 = Fs[[2]]; H1 = Hs[[1]];\n(* tensor of a product N = Bk2[F,G] <Q^3 H> as an array over (minor, r) *)\nprodTensor[F_, G_, H_] := Outer[Times, wedge2[F, G], H];\nevalTensor[cc_] := Sum[cc[[i, j]] minSym[mnL[[i]]] qq[3, rrL[[j]] ], {i, 6}, {j, 4}];\nchecks[\"Bk2[F,G] <Q3 H> = sum (F^G)_{nn'} H_r minor23 q3(r)\"] = Expand[Bk2[F1, G1] brQ[3, H1] - evalTensor[prodTensor[F1, G1, H1]]] === 0;\n(* the L=1-type 3x3: columns (<Q3 F_i>, <Q2 F_i>, <Q3 H_i>) *)\ndet3 = Det[Table[{brQ[3, Fs[[i]]], brQ[2, Fs[[i]]], brQ[3, Hs[[i]]]}, {i, 3}]];\ncc3 = prodTensor[Fs[[2]], Fs[[3]], Hs[[1]]] - prodTensor[Fs[[1]], Fs[[3]], Hs[[2]]] + prodTensor[Fs[[1]], Fs[[2]], Hs[[3]]];\nchecks[\"3x3 det = H1 x (F2^F3) - H2 x (F1^F3) + H3 x (F1^F2)\"] = Expand[det3 - evalTensor[cc3]] === 0;\n(* Pluecker quadric and polarisation in the mnL order (12),(13),(23),(14),(24),(34) *)\npf[A_] := A[[1]] A[[6]] - A[[2]] A[[5]] + A[[3]] A[[4]];\nwedge4[A_, B_] := A[[1]] B[[6]] + A[[6]] B[[1]] - A[[2]] B[[5]] - A[[5]] B[[2]] + A[[3]] B[[4]] + A[[4]] B[[3]];\nchecks[\"Pf(F^G) = 0 and (F^G)^(F^H) = 0 identically (decomposable forms sharing F)\"] = Expand[pf[wedge2[F1, G1]]] === 0 && Expand[wedge4[wedge2[F1, G1], wedge2[F1, H1]]] === 0;\nchecks[\"wedge4[A,A] = 2 pf[A]; wedge4[A,B] = pf[A+B]-pf[A]-pf[B]\"] = With[{A = Array[aa, 6], B = Array[bb, 6]}, Expand[wedge4[A, A] - 2 pf[A]] === 0 && Expand[wedge4[A, B] - (pf[A + B] - pf[A] - pf[B])] === 0];\n(* converse sanity: a decomposable 2-form with generic data has pf = 0; a generic form does not *)\nchecks[\"Pf of a random 2-form is nonzero\"] = (pf[RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, 6]] =!= 0);\n{checks[\"Bk2[F,G] <Q3 H> = sum (F^G)_{nn'} H_r minor23 q3(r)\"], checks[\"3x3 det = H1 x (F2^F3) - H2 x (F1^F3) + H3 x (F1^F2)\"], checks[\"Pf(F^G) = 0 and (F^G)^(F^H) = 0 identically (decomposable forms sharing F)\"], checks[\"wedge4[A,A] = 2 pf[A]; wedge4[A,B] = pf[A+B]-pf[A]-pf[B]\"]}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 2 results\n\nAll four symbolic identities pass (0.03 s): Bk2[F,G] <Q3 H> = sum_{n<n'} (F^G)_{nn'} H_r minor_23(n,n') q3(r) with (F^G)_{nn'} = F_n G_n' - F_n' G_n and minor_23(n,n') = q2(n') q3(n) - q3(n') q2(n) (orientation: no sign); the 3x3 det[<Q3F_i>, <Q2F_i>, <Q3H_i>] = H1 x (F2^F3) - H2 x (F1^F3) + H3 x (F1^F2) exactly (as tensors over minor x r); Pf(F^G) = 0 and (F^G)^(F^H) = 0 identically; polarisation wedge4[A,B] = Pf(A+B) - Pf(A) - Pf(B).\n\nPluecker conventions: minors ordered (12),(13),(23),(14),(24),(34) with 1,2,3,4 = points -3,-2,-1,0; Pf(A) = A12 A34 - A13 A24 + A14 A23 = A[[1]] A[[6]] - A[[2]] A[[5]] + A[[3]] A[[4]]; A^B = A12 B34 + A34 B12 - A13 B24 - A24 B13 + A14 B23 + A23 B14. Decomposable 2-form A (Pf=0, rank 2): A = F^G with F = col_i(A)/A_ij, G = col_j(A) for any A_ij not 0. Three 2-forms in a pencil of decomposables sharing a vector satisfy pairwise ^ = 0.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 3. Exact loci for N0\n\nParametrisations. (i) Gauss chart g = exp(alpha E12) exp(beta E13) exp(gamma E23): X(c) = 3 g^-1 e3 e1^T g, i.e. a = (-beta, -gamma, 1), b = (1, alpha, beta + alpha gamma) (b.a = 0 automatically); 'genuine' = alpha beta gamma not 0. (ii) the whole cone through b = a x u. Pf = Pluecker quadric of the r=0 column; both columns are 2-forms on the four points.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Gauss chart: group element, its c-vector, and the (a,b) data *)\ngaussAB[{al_, be_, ga_}] := {{-be, -ga, 1}, {1, al, be + al ga}};\nρGauss[{al_, be_, ga_}] := MatrixExp[al Ee[1, 2]] . MatrixExp[be Ee[1, 3]] . MatrixExp[ga Ee[2, 3]];\ncGauss[p_] := (uv[1] . ρGauss[p]) . Inverse[xL1];\ngaussCheck = Union[Table[Simplify[cGauss[p] - 3 rotFromAB @@ gaussAB[p]], {p, {{2/3, -3/7, 5/4}, {1, 2, 3}, {-1/2, 5, 1/3}}}]];\nchecks[\"c(exp(al E12) exp(be E13) exp(ga E23)) = 3 c(a,b) with a=(-be,-ga,1), b=(1,al,be+al ga)\"] = gaussCheck === {ConstantArray[0, 8]};\ngaussRule = {a1 -> -gB, a2 -> -gC, a3 -> 1, b1 -> 1, b2 -> gA, b3 -> gB + gA gC};\nph0 = Factor /@ (Φvac /. gaussRule); ph1 = Factor /@ (Φ20 /. gaussRule);\n(* columns of CC0 and CC1 as 6-vectors in the order (12),(13),(23),(14),(24),(34) *)\ncolsOf[cc_] := {cc[[All, 3]], cc[[All, 4]]};  (* r = -1, r = 0; r = -3,-2 columns vanish *)\nchecks[\"CC0, CC1 columns r=-3,-2 vanish\"] = (Union[Flatten[CC0[[All, 1 ;; 2]]]] === {0}) && (Union[Flatten[CC1[[All, 1 ;; 2]]]] === {0});\n{cm1, c00} = colsOf[CC0]; {cm1b, c01} = colsOf[CC1];\n(* the three invariant polynomials, in the Gauss chart and on the whole cone (b = a x u) *)\ncross[a_, u_] := {a[[2]] u[[3]] - a[[3]] u[[2]], a[[3]] u[[1]] - a[[1]] u[[3]], a[[1]] u[[2]] - a[[2]] u[[1]]};\nauRule = Thread[{b1, b2, b3} -> cross[{a1, a2, a3}, {u1, u2, u3}]];\nPf0g = Factor[pf[c00] /. gaussRule]; Wdg = Factor[wedge4[cm1, c00] /. gaussRule];\nPf0 = Factor[pf[c00] /. auRule]; Wd = Factor[wedge4[cm1, c00] /. auRule];\nQb = 43 b2^2 - 16 b1 b3;\nchecks[\"Pf(C0 col 0) = (4/7533) a1^2 (43 b2^2 - 16 b1 b3) on b.a=0 (identity in a,u)\"] = Simplify[Pf0 - (4/7533) a1^2 (Qb /. auRule)] === 0;\nchecks[\"C0 col -1 ^ C0 col 0 = (32/7533) a1 a3 b2 b3 on b.a=0\"] = Simplify[Wd - (32/7533) a1 a3 b2 b3 /. auRule] === 0;\nchecks[\"N0 col -1 decomposable (Pf=0, automatic)\"] = Expand[pf[cm1]] === 0;\n(* (R1): col0 proportional to col-1 *)\nmat2 = Transpose[{cm1 /. gaussRule, c00 /. gaussRule}];\nminors2 = DeleteCases[Union[Factor /@ Flatten[Minors[mat2, 2]]], 0];\nsolR1 = Reduce[And @@ (# == 0 & /@ minors2), {gA, gB, gC}];\n{checks[\"C0 col -1 ^ C0 col 0 and Pf, Gauss chart\"], Pf0g, Wdg, Length[minors2], solR1}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* explicit bra functions at rational points of each locus and the 64-state verification of the bracket form of N0 (+ lambda2 N1 from the tensor) against the exact overlap *)\nidxM[i_, j_] := First[First[Position[mnL, {ptsM[[i]], ptsM[[j]]}]]];\namat[A_] := Table[Which[i == j, 0, i < j, A[[idxM[i, j]]], True, -A[[idxM[j, i]]]], {i, 4}, {j, 4}];\ndecomp[A_] := Module[{M = amat[A], ij, F, G}, If[AllTrue[A, # === 0 &], Return[{ConstantArray[0, 4], ConstantArray[0, 4]}]];\n  ij = First[Select[Tuples[Range[4], 2], #[[1]] < #[[2]] && M[[#[[1]], #[[2]]]] =!= 0 &]];\n  F = M[[All, ij[[1]]]]/M[[ij[[1]], ij[[2]]]]; G = M[[All, ij[[2]]]]; {F, G}];\ndelta[m_] := UnitVector[4, m + 4];\nrulePt[{al_, be_, ga_}] := {gA -> al, gB -> be, gC -> ga};\n(* numeric brackets with rows (2,3): <Q^j F> = sum_m F_m v_j(m) *)\nbrN[B_, j_, F_] := Sum[F[[i]] vm[B, ptsM[[i]]][[j]], {i, 4}];\nbk2N[B_, F_, G_] := brN[B, 3, F] brN[B, 2, G] - brN[B, 2, F] brN[B, 3, G];\nterm2N[B_, {F_, G_, H_}] := bk2N[B, F, G] brN[B, 3, H];\ndet3N[B_, Fs_, Hs_] := Det[Table[{brN[B, 3, Fs[[i]]], brN[B, 2, Fs[[i]]], brN[B, 3, Hs[[i]]]}, {i, 3}]];\n(* deviations are measured as max |difference| over the 64 states divided by the max |exact value| (no division by possibly vanishing values) *)\nverify[p_, formN0_] := Module[{rr = rulePt[p], cc0, cc1, cvec, ex0, vals, lhs, rhs},\n  cc0 = CC0 /. gaussRule /. rr; cc1 = CC1 /. gaussRule /. rr; cvec = rotFromAB @@ gaussAB[p];\n  ex0 = Table[brk[B, cc0, {2, 3}, 3], {B, nS}]; vals = Table[formN0[B], {B, nS}];\n  lhs = Table[exactOvl[cvec, B] Psi1[B, {2, 3}, 3], {B, nS}]; rhs = vals + λ2B Table[brk[B, cc1, {2, 3}, 3], {B, nS}];\n  {Max[Abs[vals - ex0]]/Max[Abs[ex0]], Max[Abs[lhs - rhs]]/Max[Abs[lhs]]}];\n(* ---- (R2delta): main component 16 beta + 16 alpha gamma = 43 alpha^2, point (1, 11/16, 2) ---- *)\npR2 = {1, 11/16, 2};\ncc0R2 = CC0 /. gaussRule /. rulePt[pR2];\nchecks[\"R2delta point: Pf(col 0) = 0\"] = pf[cc0R2[[All, 4]]] === 0;\n{FR2m, GR2m} = decomp[cc0R2[[All, 3]]]; {FR2z, GR2z} = decomp[cc0R2[[All, 4]]];\nformR2[B_] := term2N[B, {FR2m, GR2m, delta[-1]}] + term2N[B, {FR2z, GR2z, delta[0]}];\ndevR2 = verify[pR2, formR2];\n(* ---- (R1): alpha = beta = 0, col0 = mu col-1 ---- *)\npR1 = {0, 0, 3/2};\ncc0R1 = CC0 /. gaussRule /. rulePt[pR1];\nmuR1 = First[Select[cc0R1[[All, 4]]/Replace[cc0R1[[All, 3]], 0 -> Indeterminate, {1}], NumericQ]];\n{FR1, GR1} = decomp[cc0R1[[All, 3]]]; HR1 = delta[-1] + muR1 delta[0];\nchecks[\"R1 point: col0 = mu col-1\"] = (cc0R1[[All, 4]] - muR1 cc0R1[[All, 3]]) === ConstantArray[0, 6];\nformR1[B_] := term2N[B, {FR1, GR1, HR1}];\ndevR1 = verify[pR1, formR1];\n(* ---- (R3): beta = 0 (plane alpha, gamma free), point (1/2, 0, 3/2): F_i = delta_{-3}, delta_{-2}, delta_{-1}; H_i(r) from the columns ---- *)\npR3 = {1/2, 0, 3/2};\ncc0R3 = CC0 /. gaussRule /. rulePt[pR3];\nchecks[\"R3 point: Pf(col 0) = 0 and col-1 ^ col0 = 0\"] = pf[cc0R3[[All, 4]]] === 0 && wedge4[cc0R3[[All, 3]], cc0R3[[All, 4]]] === 0;\nFR3 = {delta[-3], delta[-2], delta[-1]};\nHR3 = {delta[-1] cc0R3[[3, 3]] + delta[0] cc0R3[[3, 4]], -(delta[-1] cc0R3[[2, 3]] + delta[0] cc0R3[[2, 4]]), delta[-1] cc0R3[[1, 3]] + delta[0] cc0R3[[1, 4]]};\nchecks[\"R3 point: rows 4..6 of both CC0 columns vanish\"] = (cc0R3[[4 ;; 6, 3 ;; 4]] === ConstantArray[0, {3, 2}]);\nformR3[B_] := det3N[B, FR3, HR3];\ndevR3 = verify[pR3, formR3];\n(* on the R2delta point col-1 ^ col0 is nonzero, so that point is not of the single-3x3 type *)\nchecks[\"R2delta point: col-1 ^ col0 (nonzero = not R3)\"] = wedge4[cc0R2[[All, 3]], cc0R2[[All, 4]]];\nStringReplace[ToString[{\"R2delta\", pR2, FR2m, GR2m, FR2z, GR2z, N[devR2, 3], \"R1\", pR1, FR1, GR1, HR1, N[devR1, 3], \"R3\", pR3, HR3, N[devR3, 3], checks[\"R2delta point: col-1 ^ col0 (nonzero = not R3)\"]}, InputForm], \"\\n\" -> \" \"]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 3 results (exact; Gauss chart g = exp(al E12) exp(be E13) exp(ga E23), (a,b) = ((-be,-ga,1), (1,al,be+al ga)))\n\nN0 columns: C0_{.,-1} = (phi1, phi2, phi3, 0,0,0) = (1/3, 16 al/81, -8 (be+al ga)/27, 0,0,0) lives on {-3,-2,-1}; C0_{.,0} = (phi4, phi5, phi7, phi6, phi8, 0) with phi6 = -4 al be/93, phi8 = 8 be (be+al ga)/93; the slot (-1,0;.) is never populated (so C1_{.,-1} ^ C0_{.,0} = 0 automatically).\n\n| object | exact polynomial (Gauss chart) | on the whole cone (b = a x u) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Pf(C0_{.,0}) | -(4/7533) be^2 (16 be + 16 al ga - 43 al^2) | (4/7533) a1^2 (43 b2^2 - 16 b1 b3) |\n| C0_{.,-1} ^ C0_{.,0} | -(32/7533) al be (be + al ga) | (32/7533) a1 a3 b2 b3 |\n\n**(R2delta): Pf = 0.** Components: {a1 = 0} (be = 0: g = exp(al E12) exp(ga E23), 3-dim cone = 2-parameter family of rotations; degenerate) and {43 b2^2 = 16 b1 b3} (the quadric depends on b alone: b on a conic; 3-dim cone, 2-parameter family; contains the genuine rotations). Parametrisation of the genuine component: b = (1, al, 43 al^2/16), a = (-al (43 al/16 - ga), -ga, 1), i.e. be = al (43 al/16 - ga), (al, ga) free. It is a hypersurface of the 4-dim rotation cone, so it does not contain the cone. Test point (1, 11/16, 2): all Gauss parameters nonzero.\n\n**(R1): C0_{.,0} proportional to C0_{.,-1}** (all nine 2x2 minors, exact Reduce): only al = be = 0 (g = exp(ga E23): a = (0,-ga,1), b = (1,0,0)), a 1-parameter family; degenerate, no genuine rotation.\n\n**(R3): Pf = 0 and C0_{.,-1} ^ C0_{.,0} = 0.** Exhaustive case analysis on the cone: {a1 = 0} (the plane be = 0 in the Gauss chart, parameters al, ga) union {a3 = 0, 43 b2^2 = 16 b1 b3} (2-dim cone at infinity of the Gauss chart, parametrised a = (16 t, -43 s, 0), b = (43 s^2, 16 s t, 16 t^2)). Inside the Gauss chart with al be ga not 0 the locus is EMPTY. A single 3x3 bracket determinant of the L=1 type represents N0 only on be = 0 and on that boundary conic. The genuine (R2delta) points have C0_{.,-1} ^ C0_{.,0} not 0 (value -473/60264 at the test point).\n\n**Explicit bra functions and 64-state check.** Bra vectors over the points (-3,-2,-1,0); Bk2[F,G] = <Q3F><Q2G> - <Q2F><Q3G>; deviation = max|N0-form + lambda2 N1(tensor) - exact overlap x Psi1| / max|exact| over the 64 states (and N0-form against the N0 tensor):\n- (R2delta), point (al, be, ga) = (1, 11/16, 2): N0 = Bk2[F_-1,G_-1] q3(-1) + Bk2[F_0,G_0] q3(0) with F_-1 = {0,-1,-16/27,0}, G_-1 = {1/3,0,43/54,0}, F_0 = {0,-1,-217/873,-11/194}, G_0 = {-97/186,0,-301/432,-473/2976}. Deviations 1e-53, 1e-53.\n- (R1), point (0, 0, 3/2): F = {0,-1,0,0}, G = {1/3,0,0,0}, H = delta_-1 - (3/2) delta_0 = {0,0,1,-3/2}: N0 = Bk2[F,G] <Q3 H>. Deviations 1e-53, 1e-53.\n- (R3), point (1/2, 0, 3/2): F_i = delta_-3, delta_-2, delta_-1; H_1 = {0,0,1/3,-53/124}, H_2 = {0,0,-8/81,2/27}, H_3 = {0,0,-2/9,2/9} (rows of det[<Q3F_i>, <Q2F_i>, <Q3H_i>]). Deviations 1e-53, 1e-53.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 4. N1 and the lambda2-pencil\n\nN1 populated slots: (-3,-2;-1), (-3,-2;0), (-3,-1;0), (-2,-1;0): both columns live on the three points {-3,-2,-1}. Hence for every rotation C1_{.,-1} and C1_{.,0} are decomposable (any 2-form on a 3-dim space is) and lie in the common Lambda^2 W0, W0 = span(delta_-3, delta_-2, delta_-1): (R2delta) and (R3) hold automatically for N1. The composite is the pencil A_r(lambda2) = C0_r + lambda2 C1_r.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- Task 4: N1 alone at a generic Gauss rotation, and the composite pencil ---- *)\n(* (i) N1: R2delta and R3 automatic *)\npG = {1, 2, 3}; ccG1 = CC1 /. gaussRule /. rulePt[pG]; ccG0 = CC0 /. gaussRule /. rulePt[pG];\nchecks[\"N1: Pf(col-1) = Pf(col0) = 0 and col-1 ^ col0 = 0 identically in (al,be,ga)\"] = (Simplify[pf[c01]] === 0) && (Simplify[pf[cm1b]] === 0) && (Simplify[wedge4[cm1b, c01]] === 0);\n{FN1m, GN1m} = decomp[ccG1[[All, 3]]]; {FN1z, GN1z} = decomp[ccG1[[All, 4]]];\nformN1R2[B_] := term2N[B, {FN1m, GN1m, delta[-1]}] + term2N[B, {FN1z, GN1z, delta[0]}];\ndevN1R2 = Max[Table[Abs[formN1R2[B] - brk[B, ccG1, {2, 3}, 3]], {B, nS}]]/Max[Table[Abs[brk[B, ccG1, {2, 3}, 3]], {B, nS}]];\n(* R3 shape for N1: F_i = delta_-3, delta_-2, delta_-1 and H_i(r) from the columns, as for N0 at beta = 0 *)\nH3of[cols_] := {delta[-1] cols[[1, 3]] + delta[0] cols[[2, 3]], -(delta[-1] cols[[1, 2]] + delta[0] cols[[2, 2]]), delta[-1] cols[[1, 1]] + delta[0] cols[[2, 1]]};\nHN1 = H3of[{ccG1[[All, 3]], ccG1[[All, 4]]}];\ndevN1R3 = Max[Table[Abs[det3N[B, FR3, HN1] - brk[B, ccG1, {2, 3}, 3]], {B, nS}]]/Max[Table[Abs[brk[B, ccG1, {2, 3}, 3]], {B, nS}]];\n(* (ii) composite pencil: conditions at r=0 (r=-1 automatic) *)\nPfA0 = Factor[pf[c00] /. gaussRule]; WA01 = Factor[wedge4[c00, c01] /. gaussRule];\nWA01cone = Factor[wedge4[c00, c01] /. auRule];\nsolPencilGauss = Reduce[PfA0 == 0 && WA01 == 0 && gA gB gC != 0, {gA, gB, gC}];\n(* pencil at a point of the beta = 0 locus: F_r constant, G_r(lambda) affine, all in the 3-space of the points -3,-2,-1 *)\nnvec[A_] := {A[[3]], -A[[2]], A[[1]]};\ncr3[x_, y_] := {x[[2]] y[[3]] - x[[3]] y[[2]], x[[3]] y[[1]] - x[[1]] y[[3]], x[[1]] y[[2]] - x[[2]] y[[1]]};\npP = {1/2, 0, 3/2}; ccP0 = CC0 /. gaussRule /. rulePt[pP]; ccP1 = CC1 /. gaussRule /. rulePt[pP];\npencilFG[r_] := Module[{n0 = nvec[ccP0[[;; 3, r]]], n1 = nvec[ccP1[[;; 3, r]]], Fc}, Fc = cr3[n0, n1];\n   If[Fc === {0, 0, 0}, Fc = First[Select[{{1, 0, 0}, {0, 1, 0}, {0, 0, 1}}, cr3[n0, #] =!= {0, 0, 0} &]]];\n   {Append[Fc, 0], Function[l, Append[cr3[n0 + l n1, Fc]/(Fc . Fc), 0]]}];\n{FPm, GPm} = pencilFG[3]; {FPz, GPz} = pencilFG[4];\nformPencil[B_] := term2N[B, {FPm, GPm[λ2B[[B]]], delta[-1]}] + term2N[B, {FPz, GPz[λ2B[[B]]], delta[0]}];\ncvecP = rotFromAB @@ gaussAB[pP];\ndevPencil = Max[Table[Abs[exactOvl[cvecP, B] Psi1[B, {2, 3}, 3] - formPencil[B]], {B, nS}]]/Max[Table[Abs[exactOvl[cvecP, B] Psi1[B, {2, 3}, 3]], {B, nS}]];\npencilCheck = Table[Simplify[wedge2[{FPm, FPz}[[i]], {GPm, GPz}[[i]][l]] - (ccP0[[All, i + 2]] + l ccP1[[All, i + 2]])], {i, 2}];\n(* (iii) composite 3x3: F_i = delta's, H_i(r; lambda) affine in lambda *)\nHcomp[l_] := H3of[{ccP0[[All, 3]] + l ccP1[[All, 3]], ccP0[[All, 4]] + l ccP1[[All, 4]]}];\ndevComp3 = Max[Table[Abs[exactOvl[cvecP, B] Psi1[B, {2, 3}, 3] - det3N[B, FR3, Hcomp[λ2B[[B]]]]], {B, nS}]]/Max[Table[Abs[exactOvl[cvecP, B] Psi1[B, {2, 3}, 3]], {B, nS}]];\n(* negative control at the R2delta point: Pf of the r=0 pencil is lambda times the wedge, not 0 *)\nccQ0 = CC0 /. gaussRule /. rulePt[pR2]; ccQ1 = CC1 /. gaussRule /. rulePt[pR2];\npfPencilR2 = Factor[pf[ccQ0[[All, 4]] + l ccQ1[[All, 4]]]];\nStringReplace[ToString[{N[devN1R2, 3], N[devN1R3, 3], PfA0, WA01, WA01cone, solPencilGauss, pencilCheck, FPm, FPz, N[devPencil, 3], N[devComp3, 3], pfPencilR2}, InputForm], \"\\n\" -> \" \"]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 4 results\n\n**(i) N1.** Pf(C1_{.,-1}) = Pf(C1_{.,0}) = 0 and C1_{.,-1} ^ C1_{.,0} = 0 identically in (al,be,ga): (R2delta) and (R3) are automatic for N1. At the generic Gauss point (1,2,3) the (R2delta) form (F,G per column from `decomp`) and the (R3) form (F_i = delta_-3, delta_-2, delta_-1, H_i read off the columns) reproduce the tensor N1 on all 64 states to 1e-53 (max|diff|/max|exact|).\n\n**(ii) Composite pencil A_r(lambda2) = C0_r + lambda2 C1_r.** r = -1: automatic (all three populated slots on {-3,-2,-1}). r = 0: Pf(C0_0) = -(4/7533) be^2 (16 be + 16 al ga - 43 al^2) and C0_0 ^ C1_0 = -(280/7533) al be^2 (be + al ga) (cone: -(280/7533) a1^2 b2 b3), Pf(C1_0) = 0. Decomposable for all lambda2 iff both vanish: in the Gauss chart with al be ga not 0 the solution set is EMPTY (exact Reduce: False); on the cone it is {a1 = 0} (be = 0) union {b proportional to e3} (a3 = 0, a 2-dim cone at infinity). So no genuine rotation has N0 + lambda2 N1 as sum_{r=-1,0} det2[F_r(lambda2), G_r(lambda2)] q3(r) with delta point measures for the Q3 factor. Negative control at the genuine R2delta point (1,11/16,2): Pf(C0_0 + lambda C1_0) = -(182105/3856896) lambda, nonzero for all lambda not 0 (N0 alone is R2delta, N0 + lambda2 N1 is not).\n\nOn the locus be = 0 (plane in (al,ga)), point (1/2, 0, 3/2): F_-1 = (6790/203391, -3395/45198, 0, 0), F_0 = (35/1458, -35/486, 0, 0) (constant), G_-1(l) = ((3661038/329315)(1/3 - 3395 l/10044), (1627128/329315)(1/3 - 3395 l/10044), 10044/3395, 0), G_0(l) = ((2187/175)(-53/124 + 35 l/108), (729/175)(-53/124 + 35 l/108), -108/35, 0): affine in lambda2; F^G_r(l) = C0_r + l C1_r checked symbolically in l (residual 0). Full overlap identity on 64 states: 1e-53.\n\n**(iii) Composite 3x3**: all four 2-forms lie in Lambda^2 W for the common 3-space W = W0 only when C0_0 does, i.e. phi6 = phi8 = 0, i.e. be = 0 (same locus). There det[<Q3F_i>, <Q2F_i>, <Q3H_i(lambda2)>] with F_i = delta_-3, delta_-2, delta_-1 and H_i affine in lambda2 reproduces the full overlap on 64 states to 1e-53 (point (1/2,0,3/2)). Nothing for genuine rotations.\n\nNote: the check `pencilCheck` in the code cell above prints a non-zero residual because the symbol `l` collides with the Table iterator inside `wedge2`; it is re-done with the symbol `ll` in the Task 5 cell and gives 0 (both columns).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 5. Natural measures (report only)\n\nNatural bra: F_m = wgt4(m) rho^m (p + q m) on the four points m = -3..0 (rho = 1/w, p + q m the linear polynomial in x_m = theta1 + m h, wgt4(m) = 1/prod_{m' != m} (m' - m) h): two projective parameters (rho, q/p). Plane of a decomposable 2-form column: natural vectors in the plane are the common solutions of the 3x3 minors of {F_nat, F, G}: finitely many. Same-w test: the whole plane lies in V_rho = {rho^m (p + q m)} (recurrence s_{m+2} - 2 rho s_{m+1} + rho^2 s_m = 0 for both basis vectors). Delta/shift dictionary: the plane contains a vector supported on the pair {i,j} iff the Pluecker coordinate on the complementary pair vanishes.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "wgt4[m_] := 1/Product[(mp - m) hN, {mp, DeleteCases[ptsM, m]}];\nnatVec[ρ_, t_] := Table[wgt4[m] ρ^(m + 3) (1 + t m), {m, ptsM}];\nnatVec0[ρ_] := Table[wgt4[m] ρ^(m + 3) m, {m, ptsM}];  (* p = 0 chart *)\nnatIn[F0_, G0_] := Module[{eqs, eqs0, s1, s0},\n  eqs = DeleteCases[Union[Numerator[Together[#]] & /@ Flatten[Minors[{natVec[ρ, t], F0, G0}, 3]]], 0]; eqs0 = DeleteCases[Union[Numerator[Together[#]] & /@ Flatten[Minors[{natVec0[ρ], F0, G0}, 3]]], 0];\n  s1 = Quiet[Reduce[And @@ (# == 0 & /@ eqs) && ρ != 0, {ρ, t}]]; s0 = Quiet[Reduce[And @@ (# == 0 & /@ eqs0) && ρ != 0, {ρ}]];\n  {s1, s0}];\nsameW[F0_, G0_] := Module[{rec = Function[{vec}, With[{s = vec/Table[wgt4[m], {m, ptsM}]}, {s[[3]] - 2 ρ s[[2]] + ρ^2 s[[1]], s[[4]] - 2 ρ s[[3]] + ρ^2 s[[2]]}]]},\n   Quiet[Reduce[And @@ (# == 0 & /@ Join[rec[F0], rec[G0]]), {ρ}]]];\nzeroSupports[A_] := Map[Complement[ptsM, mnL[[#]]] &, Select[Range[6], A[[#]] === 0 &]];\n(* R2delta genuine point (1, 11/16, 2) *)\nnatR2 = {natIn[FR2m, GR2m], natIn[FR2z, GR2z]};\nsameR2 = {sameW[FR2m, GR2m], sameW[FR2z, GR2z]};\nsuppR2 = {zeroSupports[cc0R2[[All, 3]]], zeroSupports[cc0R2[[All, 4]]]};\n(* real roots of the col-0 cubic, to see how many natural vectors are real *)\ncubicRoots = NSolve[6984 ρ^3 + 3472 ρ^2 - 8143 ρ - 4257 == 0, ρ];\n(* N1 columns at (1,2,3): natural vectors in the planes *)\nnatN1 = {natIn[FN1m, GN1m], natIn[FN1z, GN1z]};\n(* the two p = 0 natural vectors of column -1 span its plane *)\nrho1 = (-32 + Sqrt[7990])/54; rho2 = (-32 - Sqrt[7990])/54;\nchecks[\"col -1 plane spanned by the two natural vectors (wedge prop. to the column)\"] = AllTrue[Flatten[Minors[{wedge2[natVec0[rho1], natVec0[rho2]], cc0R2[[All, 3]]}, 2]], PossibleZeroQ];\n(* pencil check of Task 4 redone with the symbol ll (the symbol l clashes with the Table iterator inside wedge2) *)\npencilCheck2 = Table[Simplify[wedge2[{FPm, FPz}[[i]], {GPm, GPz}[[i]][ll]] - (ccP0[[All, i + 2]] + ll ccP1[[All, i + 2]])], {i, 2}];\nStringReplace[ToString[{natR2, sameR2, suppR2, N[cubicRoots, 5], natN1, checks[\"col -1 plane spanned by the two natural vectors (wedge prop. to the column)\"], pencilCheck2}, InputForm], \"\\n\" -> \" \"]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 5 results (exact, at the genuine R2delta point (1, 11/16, 2) and at (1,2,3) for N1)\n\n- **R2delta, column r=-1** (plane spanned by F=(0,-1,-16/27,0), G=(1/3,0,43/54,0), lies in the hyperplane F_0 = 0): natural vectors exist only of the type p = 0 (F_m = wgt4(m) rho^m m): rho = (-32 +- sqrt 7990)/54 (two real, distinct). So F and G CAN be chosen natural, with DIFFERENT w (rho_1 rho_2 not equal); verified that the two natural vectors span the plane. Same-w (plane contained in V_rho): impossible (Reduce: False).\n- **R2delta, column r=0:** natural vectors of type p not 0: three, rho = the real roots of 6984 rho^3 + 3472 rho^2 - 8143 rho - 4257 = 0 (-1.0547, -0.5310, 1.0885) with q/p = t = (297 + 434 rho)/297; any two give a natural pair with different w. Same-w: False.\n- **Delta/shift dictionary:** column -1 contains vectors supported on each of the pairs {-2,-1}, {-3,-1}, {-3,-2} (because C_{14} = C_{24} = C_{34} = 0), so it is a product of two 2-point (shift-type) bras; column 0 contains one 2-point vector, supported on {-3,-2} (C_{34} = 0 only), and no other.\n- **N1 at (1,2,3):** column -1 plane = span(delta_-3, delta_-2): no natural vector at finite w (only the delta limits rho -> 0). Column 0: no p not 0 type vector, two p = 0 type: rho = 2(-27 +- sqrt 109)/31.\n- **R3 (beta = 0):** all F_i live in the 3-space W0 = {F_0 = 0} (p = 0 curve rho^m m wgt4(m): choose three distinct rho), and the freedom F_i -> M F_i, H_i -> M H_i (det M = 1) keeps the 3x3 det fixed, so natural F_i exist (any three rho); H_i is supported on {-1,0} and cannot be natural (a p + q m profile vanishing at m = -3,-2 vanishes identically).\n- Same w for both bras of a column is not available on the main locus at the tested point (the conditions would be codimension 3 in the Grassmannian of planes against a 2-parameter locus).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 7. What the loci give for CG (markdown only, no chain run)\n\nP_phys = Pmp . diag(s) . Ppp (3x3 version of `Pph1`), P^-1 = L0 D0 U0 (lower, diagonal, upper unipotent). Since e1^T rho(L) = e1^T for lower unipotent L and rho(D) is diagonal, e1^T rho(P^-1) = s e1^T rho(U0) with s = rho(D0)_{11}. The diagonal-frame covector of Phi(g) is e1^T rho(g P^-1) x e1^T rho(P^-1); the site-1 covector relative to the site-2 vacuum x0^(1) = e1^T rho(U0) is e1^T rho(g L0 D0) = e1^T rho(g L0) rho(D0) (the diagonal D0 only rescales components, so the reached weights are those of e1^T rho(g L0)).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "Ppp3 = MatrixExp[(1/zN[[1]]) ee[1, 2]] . MatrixExp[-(1/(zN[[1]] zN[[2]])) ee[1, 3]] . MatrixExp[((zN[[1]] + zN[[2]])/(zN[[1]] zN[[2]])) ee[2, 3]];\nPmp3 = MatrixExp[(r[1] /. rsN) ee[3, 2]] . MatrixExp[(r[2] /. rsN) ee[3, 1]] . MatrixExp[(r[3] /. rsN) ee[2, 1]];\nsv3 = {s[1], s[2], s[3]} /. rsN;\nP3 = Pmp3 . DiagonalMatrix[sv3] . Ppp3; P3inv = Inverse[P3];\n(* representation of a 3x3 lower / upper unipotent and diagonal *)\nrhoLow[L_] := MatrixExp[L[[2, 1]] Ee[2, 1]] . MatrixExp[L[[3, 1]] Ee[3, 1]] . MatrixExp[L[[3, 2]] Ee[3, 2]];\nrhoUp[U_] := MatrixExp[U[[1, 2]] Ee[1, 2]] . MatrixExp[(U[[1, 3]] - U[[1, 2]] U[[2, 3]]) Ee[1, 3]] . MatrixExp[U[[2, 3]] Ee[2, 3]];\nrhoDiag[d_] := DiagonalMatrix[Table[Product[d[[k]]^J0[k][p], {k, 3}], {p, ps[{Λ}]}]];\n(* L D U of P^-1 by Gaussian elimination without pivoting *)\nMg = P3inv; l21 = Mg[[2, 1]]/Mg[[1, 1]]; Mg[[2]] = Mg[[2]] - l21 Mg[[1]]; l31 = Mg[[3, 1]]/Mg[[1, 1]]; Mg[[3]] = Mg[[3]] - l31 Mg[[1]]; l32 = Mg[[3, 2]]/Mg[[2, 2]]; Mg[[3]] = Mg[[3]] - l32 Mg[[2]];\nL0 = {{1, 0, 0}, {l21, 1, 0}, {l31, l32, 1}}; Uprime = Mg; D0 = Diagonal[Uprime]; U0 = Inverse[DiagonalMatrix[D0]] . Uprime;\nchecks[\"P^-1 = L0 D0 U0, leading minors nonzero\"] = (L0 . DiagonalMatrix[D0] . U0 === P3inv) && (Times @@ D0 =!= 0);\nchecks[\"rho(P^-1) = PphInv1 (exact)\"] = Simplify[PphInv1 - rhoLow[L0] . rhoDiag[D0] . rhoUp[U0]] === ConstantArray[0, {8, 8}];\nxdiag = uv[1] . PphInv1; xU = uv[1] . rhoUp[U0];\nchecks[\"e1^T rho(P^-1) = rho(D0)_11 e1^T rho(U0) (exact)\"] = (xdiag == rhoDiag[D0][[1, 1]] xU);\n(* undone site-1 covector at a Gauss point *)\nwtL1 = Table[Table[J0[k][p], {k, 3}], {p, ps[{Λ}]}];\nundone[p_] := uv[1] . ρGauss[p] . rhoLow[L0] . rhoDiag[D0];\nidx111 = Flatten[Position[wtL1, {1, 1, 1}]];\nreach[pts_] := Module[{us = undone /@ pts}, {Union[Flatten[Table[wtL1[[k]], {u, us}, {k, Flatten[Position[u, x_ /; x =!= 0, {1}, Heads -> False]]}], 1]], MatrixRank[us[[All, idx111]]], Length[Union[Flatten[Position[#, x_ /; x =!= 0, {1}, Heads -> False]] & /@ us]], Length[Union[Flatten[Table[Flatten[Position[u, x_ /; x =!= 0, {1}, Heads -> False]], {u, us}]]]]}];\nbeta2[al_, ga_] := {al, al (43 al/16 - ga), ga};\nptsR2 = {beta2[1, 2], beta2[1/2, -1], beta2[2, 1/3]};\nptsR3 = {{1/2, 0, 3/2}, {1, 0, -1}, {2, 0, 3}};\nptsR1 = {{0, 0, 1/2}, {0, 0, 3/2}, {0, 0, -2}};\nptsGen = {{1, 2, 3}, {1/2, 1/3, 2}, {2, -1, 1/2}};\nchecks[\"points lie on their loci\"] = (And @@ (Simplify[pf[(CC0 /. gaussRule /. rulePt[#])[[All, 4]]]] === 0 & /@ ptsR2)) && (And @@ (#[[2]] === 0 & /@ ptsR3)) && (And @@ (#[[1]] === 0 && #[[2]] === 0 & /@ ptsR1));\nreachTab = {\"R2delta (genuine)\" -> reach[ptsR2], \"R3 / pencil (be = 0)\" -> reach[ptsR3], \"R1 (al = be = 0)\" -> reach[ptsR1], \"generic rotation (control)\" -> reach[ptsGen]};\n(* each reach entry: {union of site-1 weights reached, rank of the (1,1,1) components over the 3 points, # distinct GT states reached (union)} *)\n{Take[Normal[checks], -4], idx111, wtL1[[idx111]], reachTab}",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 7 results (exact, finite twist z = (3/2, 5/4, 2/3), h = 1/2, theta = (2/7, -3/5))\n\nExact checks: P3^-1 = L0 D0 U0 with L0 = {{1,0,0},{-23/12,1,0},{5/6,-2/3,1}}, D0 = diag(1, -1/4, 35/72), U0 = {{1,1,1},{0,1,10/3},{0,0,1}} (Gaussian elimination without pivoting; leading minors nonzero); rho(L0) rho(D0) rho(U0) = PphInv1 exactly; e1^T rho(P^-1) = rho(D0)_11 e1^T rho(U0) exactly (rho(D0)_11 = 1 since D0_11 = 1), so x0^(1) = e1^T rho(U0) with U0 upper unipotent exists at this z.\n\nUndone site-1 covector e1^T rho(g L0 D0) at three rational Gauss points of each locus (R2delta: (al,ga) = (1,2), (1/2,-1), (2,1/3) with be = al (43 al/16 - ga); R3/pencil be = 0: (1/2,3/2), (1,-1), (2,3); R1: al = be = 0, ga = 1/2, 3/2, -2; control: generic (1,2,3), (1/2,1/3,2), (2,-1,1/2)). The site-1 adjoint has weights (2,1,0), (2,0,1), (1,2,0), (1,0,2), (0,2,1), (0,1,2) and (1,1,1) (multiplicity 2: GT states 4 and 5).\n\n| locus | weights reached (union over 3 points) | # GT states hit (union) | nonzero components per point | rank on (1,1,1) (max 2) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| R2delta genuine | all 7: (0,1,2),(0,2,1),(1,0,2),(1,1,1),(1,2,0),(2,0,1),(2,1,0) | 8 of 8 | 8, 8, 8 | 2 |\n| R3 / pencil (be = 0) | (1,0,2),(1,1,1),(1,2,0),(2,0,1),(2,1,0) (not (0,1,2),(0,2,1)) | 6 | 2, 6, 6 | 1 |\n| R1 (al = be = 0) | (2,0,1),(2,1,0) | 2 | 2, 1, 2 | 0 |\n| generic rotation (control) | all 7 | 8 | 8, 8, 5 | 2 |\n\nSo the (R2delta) genuine family reaches everything a generic rotation does at this twist; the (R3)/pencil locus loses the two lowest weights and has only a 1-dim span on the zero-weight space; (R1) never reaches (1,1,1).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
