   "value": "## 6. z-independence and other (h, theta)\n\nDriver below re-reads the source of the setup cells from this file, substitutes the parameter line of cell 3 and re-evaluates (it wipes Global`, so it must be run LAST; afterwards re-run cells 3-31 to restore). It keeps its own helper symbols in the context Hlp` (not cleared by the first cell). Results below were obtained by evaluating exactly this code in the shared kernel (VS Code did not execute cells of this notebook).",
